      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Austwell’s arrival on the railroad shifted the planned cotton gin closer to the line, abandoning earlier sea‑port plans.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://refugiocountytx.org/relocating/austwell",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In the early 1950s Austwell boasted two restaurants, three grocery stores, two gas stations, and two tractor dealerships.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://refugiocountytx.org/relocating/austwell",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "vague"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Steam tractors began appearing in the mid‑1930s, with full conversion completed by the early 1940s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://refugiocountytx.org/relocating/austwell",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "vague"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Austwell lies less than five miles from the Guadalupe River’s mouth, near the Aransas National Wildlife Refuge home to whooping cranes.",
